  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The query is a small ionized tetrahydrocarbazole N-methylamine primary carboxamide; the closest reference pramipexole is also a small basic amine with a fused bicyclic scaffold and has accepted absolute oral bioavailability >90% despite full ionization, with measurable oral exposure after extended-release dosing.",
      "card_ids": ["C01", "C76"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Other ionized small-molecule references exceed the 20% threshold: 5-HTP 49%, labetalol 63% in cirrhosis, AZD0837 22-55%, ebastine about 40%, and PF-05241328 38%.",
      "card_ids": ["C11", "C13", "C04", "C02", "C03"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L5 records show small basic amines with measurable Caco-2 absorptive permeability and OCT1-mediated uptake of a small cation, supporting that ionization does not preclude absorption.",
      "card_ids": ["C163", "C133", "C151", "C145", "C170"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "A primary-carboxamide compound with good passive permeability and low efflux ratio, plus a P-gp substrate whose oral availability was not markedly affected in Abcb1a/1b-/- mice, indicate that gut-wall efflux need not reduce F below 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C156", "C158"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L6 records for N-methylamine/primary-carboxamide small molecules show low human liver microsomal intrinsic clearance (8 µL/min/mg for M02-M04; 2.4 µL/min/mg for methylone; 4-CMC classified low clearance), indicating no affirmative high first-pass liability for the query's amine/amide motif.",
      "card_ids": ["C214", "C191", "C198", "C207", "C220"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Some tetrahydrocarbazole sulfonamide analogs show higher intrinsic clearance (e.g., 47.31 and 57 µL/min/mg), but they differ from the query by sulfonyl/acid substitution and are not direct query measurements; they do not affirmatively establish F<20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C181", "C196"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "hepatic_clearance_metabolic_stability",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C214", "C191", "C198", "C207", "C220", "C181", "C196", "C192"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct measured oral bioavailability or IV-comparator AUC for the query molecule.",
    "No query-specific hepatic clearance or metabolic-stability measurement; L6 records are for other molecules.",
    "No query-specific permeability or efflux measurement; L5 records are for other molecules.",
    "Transferability of tetrahydrocarbazole sulfonamide clearance records is limited by different substitution (sulfonyl/acid vs N-methylamine).",
    "Solubility is likely favorable but alone does not establish F>=20%."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L6 adds no direct query measurement. Low-clearance records for N-methylamine/primary-amide small molecules support limited first-pass loss, while higher-clearance tetrahydrocarbazole sulfonamide analogs are less transferable due to different substitution. The existing high prediction is retained; unresolved uncertainty is captured as moderate confidence."
}

